  "id": "sleep-psychology",
  "term": "sleep psychology",
  "definition": "Sleep psychology is the area of psychology concerned with how psychological factors contribute to the development or persistence of sleep disorders. It also involves helping with differential diagnosis and using evidence-based cognitive-behavioral assessment and interventions to prevent sleep problems and support quality of life.",
